From 7b4e21f9351ee1056ea933c09b9bc4a99f05d365 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dann frazier <dann.frazier@chainguard.dev>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:27:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Time::HiRes: do not link librt on Linux

dist/Time-HiRes/hints/linux.pl adds -lrt so that HiRes.so links
clock_nanosleep. glibc has had clock_nanosleep and the other clock_*
functions in libc since 2.17. Since 2.34, librt.so.1 is an empty stub.

Chainguard's "eco-2.28" rebuild links packages against a glibc 2.28
sysroot in /usr/lib/oldglibc. The build environment, where perl's test
suite runs, has a newer glibc.

With -lrt, HiRes.so depends on the old librt.so.1 from the sysroot. That
library needs GLIBC_PRIVATE from the old libpthread it was built with.
The newer libpthread in the build environment does not provide it, so
HiRes.so fails to load:

  Can't load '../../lib/auto/Time/HiRes/HiRes.so' for module Time::HiRes: /lib/libpthread.so.0: version `GLIBC_PRIVATE' not found (required by /usr/lib/oldglibc/usr/lib/librt.so.1)

Test::More loads Time::HiRes through Test2::API. Most of the suite
fails as a result.

Set LIBS to an empty list so HiRes.so links only libc. Written for perl
5.44.0.
---
 dist/Time-HiRes/hints/linux.pl | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dist/Time-HiRes/hints/linux.pl b/dist/Time-HiRes/hints/linux.pl
index 84ce522..c90ff57 100644
--- a/dist/Time-HiRes/hints/linux.pl
+++ b/dist/Time-HiRes/hints/linux.pl
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
-# needs to explicitly link against librt to pull in clock_nanosleep
-$self->{LIBS} = ['-lrt'];
+# clock_nanosleep has been in libc since glibc 2.17, so librt is not needed.
+$self->{LIBS} = [];
